  "dom_id": "step-q222987",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/21d3c3c28f9ef10e5ac2623724ead9593ba24dbb1f94b81ce5313f94ee7ca511.png)\n\nUse the model above to compute the following result. Express your answer as a fraction in its lowest terms.\n\n$\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{6}{7}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $4$ and $7.$ We can make a common denominator of $4\\times 7=28.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $7$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $4$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/919b2e3f87aabf375cb968e876ee19b0ce9cd6a70c41088b062459a1f4f1f133.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{21}{28}÷\\frac{24}{28}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n21÷24=\\frac{21}{24}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
